      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## SeedVR2 3B Int8 video restore / upscale\n\nTwo-step restoration. No prompt needed: the VAE latent of the input *is* the\nconditioning, so a sampler prompt does nothing here.\n\n**Wiring that matters.** `SeedVR2TemporalChunk` outputs a LATENT *list*. Both\n`SeedVR2Conditioning` and the `KSampler` must read that same list; ComfyUI runs a\nnode once per list element and repeats the last element of shorter lists, so\nconditioning built from the *whole* latent gets paired with chunk 1 and then\nrepeated, and `comfy/ldm/seedvr/model.py` rejects it with\n`conditioning shape must match latent batch/temporal/spatial dimensions`.\nDo not rewire conditioning to come off `VAEEncodeTiled`.\n\n**VRAM.** 4n+1 frames per temporal chunk; auto picks from free VRAM. The tiled\ndecode builds a full-size float32 result accumulator whenever a frame needs more\nthan one spatial tile, which is the real wall on a 12 GB card. `tile_size` is in\npixels; SeedVR2 splits the decode in latent space at `tile_size / 8`, so a 512\ntile means 64x64 latent tiles.\n\nMeasured on a 12 GB RTX 5070 Ti Laptop, 180 frames from 768x512:\n\n| scale | output | decode tile | wall clock | peak VRAM | result |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1.0 | 768x512 | (no chunking) | 147.7 s | 10090 MiB | Laplacian var 30.7 -> 61.5 |\n| 1.5 | 1152x768 | 512 | 436.6 s | 11289 MiB | mean delta 2.36/255 |\n| 2.0 | 1536x1024 | 512 | - | - | OOM in VAEDecodeTiled |\n| 2.0 | 1536x1024 | 1024 | - | - | process killed mid-decode |\n\nScale 2.0 does not fit at 180 frames on this card. Lower `scale` or shorten the\nclip for 2x.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
